WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.234
President Biden

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:04.037
overnight racing back to Washington

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.572
for debt limit negotiations.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.706
Just hours from now,

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.707
he is set to once again

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.843
meet with House Speaker Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.844
At the White House.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.779
There's less than ten days left now

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:13.980
to reach a deal and prevent

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.615
a catastrophic default.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.416
House Republicans

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.585
are demanding huge spending cuts

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.286
before the president left Japan.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.354
He told reporters

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.523
the latest proposal from the Republicans

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.926
was, quote, unacceptable.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:31.097
I can't guarantee that

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.967
they wouldn't force a default

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.969
by doing something outrageous.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.771
I can't guarantee that.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.940
I think there are some

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.710
major Republicans in the House

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.412
who know the damage

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:48.148
that it would do to the economy.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.050
And because I am president and president

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.951
is responsible for everything,

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.219
Biden would take the blame.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.721
And that's the one way to make sure

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.823
Biden is not reelected.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.991
Biden McCarthy spoke

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.758
while the president

00:00:58.758 --> 00:00:59.492
was flying home

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.060
on Air Force

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.561
One, and McCarthy called

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.263
that talk productive.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.297
We're covering all angles.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.032
Let's begin with warm Fox tracking,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.934
tracking developments on Capitol Hill

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.869
and our left signs at the White House

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.004
are let to you.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.139
The president cut his trip short,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.473
cut off

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.974
two important legs of the trip

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.242
so he could be in Washington

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.611
for what is going to happen today.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.380
What do we expect?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:20.947
Well, Poppy,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.714
President Biden

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.715
returned to Washington

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.049
in much

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.617
the same way that he left it

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.252
without any clear resolution

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:26.853
in sight

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.421
to avert a default in

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.090
as little as ten days.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.291
But a bit later today,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.525
President Biden and House Speaker

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.194
Kevin McCarthy will sit down

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.562
for another high stakes

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.162
meeting

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.063
really highlighting

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.332
the urgency of this moment.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.434
The two of them spoke on the phone

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.069
yesterday as the president

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.637
traveled back on Air Force One.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.573
And that led to negotiators

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.440
from both sides

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.109
coming to the negotiating table

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.010
last night on Capitol Hill.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.045
The two sides met

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.880
for about two and a half hours.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.014
They look to work through

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.549
some of the very vast

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.218
differences that remain

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.319
when it comes to trying

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.854
to reach a budget agreement.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.855
And one of those key

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.957
sticking points has been around

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.758
spending levels as the White House

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.593
wants to keep

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.561
spending at the current year's levels

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.762
while Republicans

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.131
want to see it cut back

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.066
and reverted back to fiscal year.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.167
2022.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.669
But but the president over the weekend

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.404
really highlighted that he believes

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.940
that the Republicans proposals recently

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.142
that were recently

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.877
put forth over the weekend

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.346
that they amount to extreme positions.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.414
And it is the White House's belief

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.415
that Republicans

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.017
need to realize

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.052
that this needs to be a bipartisan deal

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.188
which will require compromise

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.690
and some movement from GOP positions.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.392
But bottom line here,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.160
the president,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.895
Speaker McCarthy, are facing

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.696
very serious time constraints.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.497
Yesterday

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.698
We heard Treasury Secretary

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.834
Janet Yellen once again reaffirm

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.502
that she believes the U.S.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.670
could default on its debts

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.172
as early as June.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.541
First really highlighting the urgency

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.910
the fact that this is a very fast

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.645
moving situation

00:02:58.645 --> 00:02:59.979
and really that the leaders

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:00.880
that President Biden

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.314
and Speaker

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.383
McCarthy need to act very quickly

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.851
in order to avert a default.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.885
But for the time being,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.353
it's still remains

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.254
that it still appears

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.456
to be that the differences are vast.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.859
Let's go to Lauren now.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:13.960
Earlier, Poppy mentioned

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:14.527
that McCarthy

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.796
has a very narrow majority in the House.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.698
How does this impact his strategy

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.366
as he goes into this meeting?

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.202
I mean, we are at crunch time now.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.137
Yes, I

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:24.571
mean, he just

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.706
doesn't have the kind of negotiating room

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:27.440
that he would have

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.976
if he had a larger Republican majority

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.444
in the back of his mind

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.111
has to be

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.346
this reality

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.280
that he is going

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.182
to lose conservative votes

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.851
if he actually makes a bipartisan deal

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.620
with President Joe Biden.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.854
And that calculus,

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.622
whether or not

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.190
he is going to be willing

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:44.791
to potentially

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.426
put his speakership on the line

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.460
for that deal

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.162
is something that is looming large

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.730
in these negotiations.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.397
Also looming

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.499
large is the reality that these two men

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.835
have a very untested relationship.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.136
They really haven't spent that

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.972
much one on one time together.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.573
They never spent that much time

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.242
in the previous two years

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.277
when Biden was president and

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.512
you had McCarthy,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.581
who was in the minority at that point.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.250
So there is a huge question mark

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:10.683
right now,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.217
whether or not

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.218
their relationship

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.853
really can get this deal

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.121
over the finish line,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.356
like Arlette mentioned.

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:17.290
The negotiations

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.024
over the weekend

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.193
happened in fits and starts

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.295
with both sides trading back and forth.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.330
Proposals that the other side argued

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.531
were unreasonable.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.700
I talked to one Republican last night

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.036
who told me that they feel like right now

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.872
this deal is just hanging by a thread.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.506
Whether or not

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.608
they can actually find a way forward

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.543
is a major question mark.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.344
And like you noted,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.445
time is running short

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.380
to move this through.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.748
The House of Representatives

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.483
would take several days,

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.884
at least 72 hours

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.819
for members to look at a plan

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.655
and then vote on it in the Senate.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:50.490
It could take even longer.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.158
Now, that's always possible.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.127
That they could move more expeditiously.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.895
But as Kevin McCarthy

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.063
noted over the weekend,

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.531
he has been planning

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.732
for potentially the Senate

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.900
to need seven days.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.535
Maybe they need less than that.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.070
But that just gives you a sense

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.773
of how short we are running on time.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.207
Wow. Seven days.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:12.378
So ten -7 is three so that means, Lauren,

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.880
they got three days to figure this out.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.016
But that's the big question right now.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.051
And I think that it's always

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:18.785
possible things

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.320
move much more quickly in the Senate

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:20.953
when they need to.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.455
But McCarthy has been arguing

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:25.224
he thought they might need a whole week.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.159
Thank you both.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:26.993
I can't believe you're doing

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:27.660
math at this hour,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.661
but that's really good.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.195
That's what we have.

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.163
Christine Romans here

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.231
for goodness for her.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.900
My deep sighs over here.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.001
I know

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.270
you have been talking about this

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.172
ad nauseum over and over and over again,

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.807
but you said something that really sent

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:42.041
shivers down my spine.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:42.809
You said that

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.711
if we didn't pass the debt limit,

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:47.280
that we would see our living standards

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.781
go back in time.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.850
This is for every American. Yes.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.553
This is incredibly dangerous

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.554
what's happening here right now

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.388
and how close we are.

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:57.390
$56 billion in the bank this morning.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.492
And we have a bunch of bills

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.260
are going to be coming due next month.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.128
Will be money coming in

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.497
from state tax receipts and the like

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:05.231
to be playing it

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.300
this close is just really,

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.234
really dangerous

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.001
for the American economy.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.370
So what do I mean about living standards

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.371
going back in time

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.438
you could have

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.507
a 10th of economic activity just stop.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.443
The minute that they do this 10th of so

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.878
you have the Treasury Department

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:19.412
that will be having

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.613
a Hunger Games of sorts

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.781
of which bills to pay.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.182
So you're talking about IOUs

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.118
for service members. That's one option.

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.219
You could have

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:27.754
delays and Social Security checks.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.355
So think about the senior

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.023
who relies on the Social Security check,

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.625
who then can't go to the bodega

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:33.960
to buy the milk

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.161
and the bread for the week,

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.229
who then the bodega

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.497
then doesn't have that income.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:37.830
I mean,

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.565
it just starts to all go down

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.299
the food chain

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.467
and it's very dangerous

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.536
to say nothing of what it means

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.071
for financial security.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.739
Remember, the entire global

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.774
financial system

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:51.144
is built on the American Treasury bond.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.678
And this is something

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.180
that the world hungers for.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:54.514
They go

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:57.150
have they buy as safety our bonds.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.818
It's not a sign of weakness.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.286
Everybody it's a sign of strength

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.554
that the American

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:03.089
this security is so sought

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.223
after around the world,

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.558
you start to undermine the

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.325
underpinning of that.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.326
You hurt the dollar.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:07.894
Instability.

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:08.761
The dollar is very good

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.363
for America's competitors. Like China.

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:10.563
I mean,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.799
the whole thing is just a real hot mess.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.634
There are former colleague

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.835
Lydia DePillis, who's now

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:16.335
there are times

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.570
I thought we wrote a great piece

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.805
over the weekend about,

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:19.472
you know,

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.273
essentially you're

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.175
talking about our creditors.

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:24.177
And if they see us default

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:26.312
on our payments to our service members,

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.448
elderly Americans on Social Security,

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:31.050
they've got to be thinking we are next.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.686
And so that upends the whole system

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.254
of the full faith and credit of the U.S.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.456
government and

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.390
that the dollar should be

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.392
the reserve currency. Right? Exactly.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:40.760
And that's how that plays into China's

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.195
hands or plays into

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.830
the hands of competitors

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.697
who would like to see a world

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:45.765
that's not based on the dollar

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:46.632
where the US Treasury

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.367
isn't isn't the king of the hill.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.702
And it is the king of the Hill.

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:51.704
Look, the

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:52.772
US will pay

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.807
interest on its debt, I'm sure.

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:55.842
I mean debt holders.

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:57.810
I mean, that would just be devastating

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.512
if they defaulted on those obligations.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.446
But to do that,

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:03.015
you have to make big cuts and sacrifices

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:03.916
elsewhere.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.786
That just is a sign of weakness,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.621
a sign of poor planning. As I look.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.590
There is a serious discussion

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.825
about America's national debt

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:13.893
growing so large

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.661
that chokes our country

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.263
in the decades in the future.

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:17.997
That's serious.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.233
Conversation is not had around a debt

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:21.300
ceiling drama.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.502
It's had

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:24.670
serious bipartisan discussions

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.005
in the budgeting process.

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:27.306
So we're not doing that right now.

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:27.940
And I think

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:28.975
that there are some Republicans

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:29.775
and there are some Democrats

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:30.543
who think that that's what

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:31.511
we're having a conversation.

00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:32.311
We're having a conversation

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.013
about spending priorities.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.481
This is money that's already been spent.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:35.815
Right.

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:37.116
The spending priority conversation

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:37.650
has to happen

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.186
in a much more meaningful way than this.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:41.187
This is distraction.

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:42.121
This is not discipline.

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.623
This is distraction.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:44.757
This is drama.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:45.758
This is not discipline.

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:46.459
What you're seeing here,

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:47.960
I am old enough to remember

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.630
the deficit clock ticking down.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.265
We were in front of it this weekend.

00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:53.232
I went this weekend to

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.201
